completed_at: "2026-08-08T23:31:06.848Z"
claim_principal: pi-agent
author: pi-agent
acceptance_criteria: "Every spawnSync site audited and assigned a tier with justification; silent-degradation sites (itemStatus, loadAppliedByTransaction) throw a named error on a status===null overrun instead of returning empty/absent; regression test drives itemStatus past Node's 1 MiB default and asserts the real status returns; mutation-tested (reverting each fix fails its test); full gate green (typecheck, coverage thresholds unchanged, audit, pack); standalone-loadability preserved."
notes[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-08T22:59:39.151Z",pi-agent,"Acceptance evidence:\n\nGates (all green):\n- npm run typecheck: clean.\n- npm run coverage: index.ts 83.01% lines / 77.51% branches / 88.54% funcs; thresholds 81/74/88 UNCHANGED, no c8 ignore (coverage rose vs baseline 82.68/76.75/88.42).\n- npm run build: clean.\n- npm run audit:prod: 0 vulnerabilities.\n- npm run pack:dry-run: 9 files, packs.\n- Full suite: 114 tests pass (109 prior + 5 new in test/buffer-regression.test.ts).\n\nPer-call-site tier assignment (see PR body for the full table):\n- itemStatus (pm get): tier-2. Was the only read on Node's 1 MiB default AND mapped null status onto undefined (silent \"item missing\"). Now maxBuffer + assertPmOutputFit.\n- loadAppliedByTransaction (pm list-all): tier-2. Had maxBuffer (#41) but swallowed null/error into an empty applied map (silent re-import). Now assertPmOutputFit.\n- loadKeyIndex, buildCsvExport (pm list-all): tier-2. Already threw on error (#41); unchanged (loud, not silent).\n- upsertCreate create/close, upsertUpdate update/close: tier-2. Added maxBuffer + assertPmOutputFit.\n- compensateCreate update/close: tier-2. Added maxBuffer only (best-effort rollback tolerates failure by design; no assert).\n- Tier-1 (in-process SDK read) NOT used: a static @unbrained/pm-cli value import breaks documented standalone-loadability (confirmed ERR_MODULE_NOT_FOUND loading dist/ off the package resolution path); task forbids dynamic import(); ctx.sdk.client.list carries a read-output budget. Verified standalone load is PRESERVED after the fix.\n\nMutation test results (revert fix in scratch, confirm new test FAILS, restore):\n- Revert itemStatus (drop maxBuffer+assert): \"itemStatus returns the real status ... exceeds 1 MiB\" FAILS, \"itemStatus surfaces a buffer overrun as a named error\" FAILS. Restored -> pass.\n- Revert loadAppliedByTransaction assert: \"loadAppliedByTransaction surfaces a buffer overrun as a named error\" FAILS. Restored -> pass.\nBoth new tests are load-bearing (fail without the fix).\n\nRegression coverage of the fix:\n- A read path (itemStatus) driven past Node's 1 MiB default (2 MiB body via --body-file) returns the REAL status, not undefined.\n- A tier-2 site (itemStatus AND loadAppliedByTransaction) under a capped PM_LIST_MAX_BUFFER surfaces the overrun as a named error, not an empty/absent result."
  "2026-08-08T23:30:49.907Z",pi-agent,"PR #59 review follow-up — three findings (CodeRabbit Major, Greptile P1/P2). All resolved on this branch; no new PR, no merge, no bot mention.\n\nF1 (CodeRabbit, index.ts itemStatus→compensateCreate, Major): the guard now throws inside itemStatus, which compensateCreate calls, so an overrun in the compensation status lookup aborted the sweep before the best-effort strip/close subprocesses. Fix: compensateCreate catches the overrun (itemStatus's only throw is the CommandError from assertPmOutputFit; a bare catch is equivalent to catching CommandError and avoids an unreachable rethrow branch) and treats THAT row's compensation as a no-op; the sweep over the remaining applied creates continues. The hard error is kept on the import read path (loadAppliedByTransaction, the verification itemStatus in upsertCreate).\n\nF2 (Greptile P1, index.ts upsertCreate): a write overrun stranded an un-identifiable orphan. (2a) `pm create` persists the item BEFORE its receipt overruns the buffer; the old assert threw before the id was parsed, so compensation could not identify the orphan. Fix: parse the id FIRST (verified empirically that Node retains the FULL captured stdout for outputs under one read chunk, and pm create --json's flat receipt is always far under that, so the id is recoverable even on overrun); on a null status, if the id was recovered, best-effort close the orphan DIRECTLY (compensation's own status lookup would overrun under the same cap and no-op, so the close is issued here and its result tolerated) and throw a named, id-carrying error; without the id, throw naming the title for manual reconcile. (2b) the close-result assert before the close-failure branch bypassed that branch's existing compensation on a null close status; fix: drop that assert so a null close routes INTO the compensation branch (the id is already known, so nothing is stranded).\n\nF3 (Greptile P2, index.ts assertPmOutputFit): status===null is not only an overrun — a child terminated by a signal also reports it, and SIGTERM is the SAME signal a buffer-driven kill produces, so the signal alone cannot discriminate. Fix: a shared describePmNullStatus(result,label) distinguishes the three causes from the evidence Node actually populates (verified against @types/node SpawnSyncReturns AND empirically): error.code===\"ENOBUFS\" → stdout overrun (names the buffer + PM_LIST_MAX_BUFFER); error set with another code → spawn/system error (explicitly NOT a buffer problem); error unset + signal → external signal termination (explicitly NOT a buffer problem). assertPmOutputFit and the write paths both reuse it.\n\nEvidence / gates (all green):\n- npm run typecheck: clean.\n- npm run coverage: index.ts 83.62% lines / 78.42% branches / 88.66% funcs — UP vs the prior round's 83.01/77.51/88.54 and above the current floors (83.0/77.5/88.5) and thresholds (81/74/88, UNCHANGED). No c8 ignore. coverage-gate: 1 source file reported, thresholds met.\n- npm run build: clean. npm run audit:prod: 0 vulnerabilities. npm run pack:dry-run: 9 files.\n- Full suite: 121 tests pass (114 prior + 7 new: F1 + 3×F3 classifier in buffer-regression.test.ts; 3×F2 import-path in atomic.test.ts).\n\nPer-test mutation results (revert the fix in scratch, confirm the test FAILS, restore):\n- F1 (compensateCreate tolerant): revert the try/catch → F1 test FAILS (the overrun propagates out of compensateCreate). Restored → pass.\n- F3-buffer: revert describePmNullStatus to the old single message → FAILS (no ENOBUFS in the message). Restored → pass.\n- F3-signal: revert → FAILS (no \"terminated by signal\"/\"NOT a stdout buffer overrun\"). Restored → pass.\n- F3-spawn-error: revert → FAILS (no \"could not run to completion\"/ENOENT). Restored → pass.\n- F2a (overrun, id recovered, orphan closed): revert the create-site ordering (assert before parse) → FAILS (raw buffer error, no id, orphan left OPEN). Restored → pass.\n- F2a-not-recovered (create killed, title named): revert → FAILS (raw signal abort, title not named). Restored → pass.\n- F2b (null close routes into compensation): restore the close-result assert → FAILS (raw signal abort bypasses compensation, no \"left OPEN\"). Restored → pass.\nAll 7 new tests are load-bearing. The 2 updated existing tests (itemStatus / loadAppliedByTransaction overrun wording) remain load-bearing: reverting their maxBuffer+assert makes itemStatus return undefined / loadAppliedByTransaction return an empty map instead of throwing (unchanged behavior, only the asserted message wording changed).\n\nStandalone-loadability preserved: dist/index.js loads from an isolated dir with NO node_modules (only node: builtins are value-imported; @unbrained/pm-cli imports are type-only and erased). Verified the built module exports describePmNullStatus and the default extension object.\n\nEmpirical facts used by the fix (verified against node_modules/@types/node SpawnSyncReturns + a direct probe): buffer overrun → status null, signal SIGTERM, error.code===\"ENOBUFS\", stdout retained in full for outputs under one read chunk; external signal kill → status null, signal=<the signal>, error undefined, empty stdout; pm close under a tiny maxBuffer still persists the close (the write precedes the receipt emission that trips the kill)."
