  npm run coverage,project
  npm run typecheck,project
close_reason: "PR #59 review follow-up resolved on the same branch (no new PR, no merge, no bot mention). Three findings fixed: (F1) compensateCreate now catches an overrun in its own itemStatus lookup and treats that row as a no-op so the compensation sweep is not aborted, while the import read path keeps the hard error; (F2) upsertCreate parses the create id BEFORE any throw and best-effort closes a recovered orphan directly (a write that may have taken effect is never abandoned un-identified), and a null close status now routes into the close-failure compensation branch instead of bypassing it; (F3) a shared describePmNullStatus distinguishes a stdout overrun (ENOBUFS) from a spawn/system error and from an external signal kill, wording each message for its real cause (verified against @types/node SpawnSyncReturns and empirically). Gates green: typecheck clean; coverage 83.62/78.42/88.66 (up vs prior 83.01/77.51/88.54, above floors 83.0/77.5/88.5 and thresholds 81/74/88 UNCHANGED, no c8 ignore); audit 0 vulns; pack 9 files; 121 tests pass (114 prior + 7 new). All 7 new tests mutation-tested (revert fix -> fail). Standalone-loadability preserved (dist/ loads with only node: builtins)."
body: ""
